{"step_index":256,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-24T17:47:22Z","input_tokens":2529,"cache_read_tokens":141955,"output_tokens":931,"content":"### Phase 1 Execution Complete: Ground Truth Calibration & Evidence Analysis\n\nWe have completed the reverse-engineering and calibration of all 32 sample cases in [`dataset/sample_output.csv`](file:///home/skandan-c-y/PycharmProjects/hackerrank-orchestrate-october26/dataset/sample_output.csv) and calibrated the core rules:\n\n---\n\n#### 1. Identity Resolution Verification (100% Resolved)\n- **Sample Requests**: **32 / 32** resolve directly or via historical aliases to canonical `user_id`s.\n- **Evaluation Requests**: **518 / 518 (100%)** successfully resolve to canonical `user_id`s using our combined current and historical identity graph (`user_identities.csv` + `user_audit_log.csv`). No orphan identities exist.\n\n---\n\n#### 2. Discovery of the Non-Deletion Boundary (`NOT_APPLICABLE`)\n- Across the 518 evaluation requests, **cases 533 through 542 (exactly 10 cases)** represent non-deletion intents (e.g., GDPR Article 15 access requests, data portability downloads, telephone/name correction requests, marketing newsletter opt-outs, and invoice copies).\n- All 10 explicitly state to keep the account active or clarify that they are not asking for deletion.\n- Our deterministic intent filter correctly identifies:\n  - 508 cases $\\to$ Deletion requests (`COMPLETE` / `INCOMPLETE`)\n  - 10 cases (`case_533` to `case_542`) $\\to$ `NOT_APPLICABLE` with `steps_json = []`\n\n---\n\n#### 3. Evidence Selection & Temporal Invariant Calibration\nWe analyzed the 13 evidence files cited across the 32 sample cases:\n- In **100% of cases**, the cited evidence file satisfies `captured_at <= audit_at`.\n- When a comprehensive bundle/export exists (e.g., `service_resource_export`, `records_assurance_snapshot_bundle`, `customer_account_handover`, `service_readback_logs`, or `central_observability_export`), **all steps cite that single comprehensive snapshot**.\n- In component-specific captures (e.g. failover replica DB `evidence_54`, search primary DB `evidence_57`, export jobs `evidence_59`, backup inventory `evidence_93`), each system cites its respective capture.\n\n---\n\n#### 4. Step Ordering Contract Verified\nAcross all 193 ground-truth steps in `sample_output.csv`, ordering strictly follows:\n1. **Phase Priority**: `FINDING` $\\to$ `REMEDIATION` $\\to$ `VERIFICATION`\n2. **Finding Operation Priority**:\n   `REPORT_REMAINING_RECORD` $\\to$ `REPORT_EXPOSED_PII` $\\to$ `REPORT_ACTIVE_DATA_FLOW` $\\to$ `REPORT_RESTORE_RISK`\n3. **Remediation Operation Priority**:\n   `DISABLE_DATA_FLOW` $\\to$ `BLOCK_RESTORE` $\\to$ `DELETE_RECORD` $\\to$ `REDACT_RECORD` $\\to$ `ANONYMIZE_RECORD`\n4. **Verification Operation Priority**:\n   `VERIFY_RECORD_ABSENT` $\\to$ `VERIFY_RECORD_PRESENT` $\\to$ `VERIFY_RECORD_REDACTED` $\\to$ `VERIFY_RECORD_ANONYMIZED` $\\to$ `VERIFY_DATA_FLOW_DISABLED` $\\to$ `VERIFY_RESTORE_BLOCKED`\n5. **Tie-Breaker**: `system_id` ascending $\\to$ `resource_id` ascending.\n\n---\n\n### Ready for Phase 2\nPhase 1 calibration is complete and verified. Next is **Phase 2: Core Engine Development**, writing the end-to-end pipeline in [`code/main.py`](file:///home/skandan-c-y/PycharmProjects/hackerrank-orchestrate-october26/code/main.py). Shall we proceed?"}
